ath Proficiency Exams\nGraduate\nFrequently Asked Questions\nAdmission\nFinancial Aid\nMasters and PhD Requirements\nIntegrated Graduate Studies Program\nGraduate Courses\nMathematics Graduate Student Association\nDirected Reading Program\nCareers\nNews & Events\nNews and Events\nDepartment of MAMS Newsletter\nColloquia\nUpcoming Colloquia\nPast Colloquia\nSeminars\nUpcoming Seminars\nPast Seminars\nDataFest\nDataFest 2025\nDataFest 2024\nDataFest 2023\nDataFest 2020\nDataFest 2019\nDataFest 2018\nDataFest 2017\nDataFest FAQ\nDataFest Testimonials\nPast Sponsors\nThe annual Elizabeth S. Meckes Memorial Lecture\nPublic Lecture\nStudent Presentations\nPast Student Presentations\nResearch\nResearch Areas\nPublications\nPresentations\nResources\nUndergraduate Student Resources\nGraduate Student Resources\nFaculty Resources\nGiving\nHome \u00bb Admission \u00bb Financial Aid\nFinancial Aid\nThe department awards several teaching and research assistantships to PhD students each year. Recipients of teaching assistantships are expected to teach or assist with the instructional work of the department. All assistantship awards include tuition and stipend to cover basic living expenses. The stipends vary according to the nature of the award but are comparable to those of other graduate schools. At this time, support is only available to a select number PhD students. We do not offer support for MS students.\nThere is no separate application form for an assistantship. To be certain of consideration for financial aid for the following academic year, an applicant must have all application material on file by January 15. Late applications will be considered only if there are still graduate assistantships which have not been awarded.\nDepartment of Mathematics, Applied Mathematics and Statistics\nCase Western Reserve University\nLocation 1: 2145 Adelbert Rd.\nLocation 2: Sears 5th Floor\n2083 Martin Luther King Jr Dr\nCleveland, OH 44106-7058\nLegal Notice | Privacy Policy\nTitle IX